From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hamed7ir <hamedghorbani17@live.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [clang][ARM] Use sponentry for setjmp on Windows ARM32 (D42)

Port of upstream/patches/0001-D42-arm32-windows-setjmp-sponentry.patch to the
18.1.8 tree. The two source hunks are identical in content to the upstream draft;
only the line numbers differ (1376/1393 here, 1780/1797 on main).

On Windows, _setjmp and _setjmpex take a second argument, the frame, which the CRT
stores into the jmp_buf and which longjmp later hands to RtlUnwindEx as the frame to
unwind to. EmitMSVCRTSetJmp computes that argument with llvm.sponentry -- the stack
pointer as it was on entry to the function -- but only when the target architecture
is aarch64. 32-bit x86's _setjmp goes to _setjmp3 instead; every other case falls
through to llvm.frameaddress(0) and passes the frame pointer, 32-bit Arm included.

On 32-bit Arm the frame pointer is r11, and a function that sets one up leaves it
pointing at its own saved slot. r11 and lr are the two highest-numbered registers in
a callee-save push, so that slot is always the second from the top of the push:
8 bytes below the stack pointer on entry. MSVC for the same target passes the stack
pointer at function entry.

MEASURED for this port (scratch/SJ1, and recorded in SETJMP-1-RESULTS.md):

  - 7 clang builds spanning 18.1.8 through main all emit `mov r1, r11`, i.e.
    r1 - entrySP = -8. Three MSVC ARM32 toolsets spanning 2018 to 2025 all emit
    `add r1, sp, #N` resolving to r1 - entrySP = 0.
  - The defect is not introduced by any rt1 patch: stock official 18.1.8 from
    C:\Program Files\LLVM produces a `probe` function byte-identical to rt1.1's.
  - No backend work sits behind this change. llvm/test/CodeGen/ARM/sponentry.ll
    already exists IN THIS TREE, runs llc -mtriple=thumbv7-windows-msvc over IR that
    hands llvm.sponentry to _setjmpex, and expects `add.w r1, r11, #8`. It PASSES on
    the unpatched rt1.1 compiler. The backend half is not merely present, it is
    already tested for this exact target; only the frontend condition was left behind.
    (llvm.sponentry was added for AArch64 Windows in D53673, for this same argument.)

The AArch64 half is left spelled getArch() == Triple::aarch64 rather than folded into
Triple::isAArch64(), so the change is a pure extension: every triple that reaches this
code keeps the value it gets today and only arm/armeb/thumb/thumbeb move. isAArch64()
would also match aarch64_be, and that is not hypothetical -- clang today emits
llvm.frameaddress for aarch64_be-pc-windows-msvc, so spelling it that way would quietly
change codegen for a target this patch has no business touching.

DELIBERATELY NOT TOUCHED: the callee selector in EmitBuiltinExpr, which sends aarch64
to the _setjmpex kind and leaves 32-bit Arm on _setjmp. Post-patch ARM32 therefore
still calls @_setjmp, and that is correct and intended here -- MSVC's own setjmp.h
maps setjmp to _setjmp on every architecture unless <setjmpex.h> is included, and the
CRT's _setjmp tail-jumps into setjmpex with r0/r1 intact when _setjmpexused is set.
Changing that selector is a separate question (tracked as D43) and would widen a
codegen fix into an unreviewed runtime-ABI change. Do not "fix" it while here.

The test's ARM32 CHECK block is written from measured ARM32 output, NOT copied from the
AARCH64 block: the ARM32 label carries arm_aapcs_vfpcc and the callee is @_setjmp, not
@_setjmpex. Both armv7 and thumbv7 RUN lines are present because the new condition has
two arms -- armv7-*-windows-msvc canonicalises to Triple::thumb, so isThumb() is the
load-bearing half, and a test exercising only one arm would let the other be deleted
green.

SEEN TO FAIL BEFORE SEEN TO PASS. On the unpatched compiler (build/bin/clang.exe,
sha256 f3541308...), the test's 10 RUN lines were executed individually from the
shipped file: the 6 pre-existing lines PASS and all 4 new ARM32 lines FAIL, each on
`%0 = call ptr @llvm.frameaddress.p0(i32 0)` where the ARM32 prefix requires
@llvm.sponentry.p0(). Evidence: scratch/SJ2/must-fail/UNPATCHED-summary.txt.

DIFFERENCE FROM THE UPSTREAM DRAFT: that draft also edits clang/docs/ReleaseNotes.md.
This port omits it. 18.1.8 ships ReleaseNotes.rst rather than .md, and none of rt1's
patches 0001-0009 touch release notes -- rt1 is a frozen one-shot overlay, not a
release line. The note belongs to the upstream filing, which already carries it.

Found on 32-bit Windows on Arm, where a longjmp in a program built with clang-cl dies
with STATUS_BAD_STACK (0xC0000028) on device while the same program built with MSVC
runs to completion.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5 (Anthropic)
---
 clang/lib/CodeGen/CGBuiltin.cpp | 11 +++++++----
 clang/test/CodeGen/ms-setjmp.c  | 14 ++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGBuiltin.cpp b/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGBuiltin.cpp
--- a/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGBuiltin.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGBuiltin.cpp
@@ -1376,9 +1376,11 @@
 };
 }
 
-/// MSVC handles setjmp a bit differently on different platforms. On every
-/// architecture except 32-bit x86, the frame address is passed. On x86, extra
-/// parameters can be passed as variadic arguments, but we always pass none.
+/// MSVC handles setjmp a bit differently on different platforms. On 32-bit x86
+/// extra parameters can be passed as variadic arguments, but we always pass
+/// none. Everywhere else a frame value is passed: the stack pointer as it was
+/// on entry to the function for AArch64 and 32-bit Arm, and the frame address
+/// for the rest.
 static RValue EmitMSVCRTSetJmp(CodeGenFunction &CGF, MSVCSetJmpKind SJKind,
                                const CallExpr *E) {
   llvm::Value *Arg1 = nullptr;
@@ -1393,7 +1395,8 @@
   } else {
     Name = SJKind == MSVCSetJmpKind::_setjmp ? "_setjmp" : "_setjmpex";
     Arg1Ty = CGF.Int8PtrTy;
-    if (CGF.getTarget().getTriple().getArch() == llvm::Triple::aarch64) {
+    const llvm::Triple &T = CGF.getTarget().getTriple();
+    if (T.getArch() == llvm::Triple::aarch64 || T.isARM() || T.isThumb()) {
       Arg1 = CGF.Builder.CreateCall(
           CGF.CGM.getIntrinsic(Intrinsic::sponentry, CGF.AllocaInt8PtrTy));
     } else
diff --git a/clang/test/CodeGen/ms-setjmp.c b/clang/test/CodeGen/ms-setjmp.c
--- a/clang/test/CodeGen/ms-setjmp.c
+++ b/clang/test/CodeGen/ms-setjmp.c
@@ -1,9 +1,13 @@
 // RUN: %clang_cc1 -fms-extensions -DDECLARE_SETJMP -triple i686-windows-msvc   -emit-llvm %s -o - | FileCheck --check-prefix=I386 %s
 // RUN: %clang_cc1 -fms-extensions -DDECLARE_SETJMP -triple x86_64-windows-msvc -emit-llvm %s -o - | FileCheck --check-prefix=X64 %s
 // RUN: %clang_cc1 -fms-extensions -DDECLARE_SETJMP -triple aarch64-windows-msvc -emit-llvm %s -o - | FileCheck --check-prefix=AARCH64 %s
+// RUN: %clang_cc1 -fms-extensions -DDECLARE_SETJMP -triple thumbv7-windows-msvc -emit-llvm %s -o - | FileCheck --check-prefix=ARM32 %s
+// RUN: %clang_cc1 -fms-extensions -DDECLARE_SETJMP -triple armv7-windows-msvc   -emit-llvm %s -o - | FileCheck --check-prefix=ARM32 %s
 // RUN: %clang_cc1 -fms-extensions -triple i686-windows-msvc -Wno-implicit-function-declaration -emit-llvm %s -o - | FileCheck --check-prefix=I386 %s
 // RUN: %clang_cc1 -fms-extensions -triple x86_64-windows-msvc -Wno-implicit-function-declaration -emit-llvm %s -o - | FileCheck --check-prefix=X64 %s
 // RUN: %clang_cc1 -fms-extensions -triple aarch64-windows-msvc -Wno-implicit-function-declaration -emit-llvm %s -o - | FileCheck --check-prefix=AARCH64 %s
+// RUN: %clang_cc1 -fms-extensions -triple thumbv7-windows-msvc -Wno-implicit-function-declaration -emit-llvm %s -o - | FileCheck --check-prefix=ARM32 %s
+// RUN: %clang_cc1 -fms-extensions -triple armv7-windows-msvc -Wno-implicit-function-declaration -emit-llvm %s -o - | FileCheck --check-prefix=ARM32 %s
 typedef char jmp_buf[1];
 
 #ifdef DECLARE_SETJMP
@@ -28,6 +32,11 @@
   // AARCH64:       %[[addr:.*]] = call ptr @llvm.sponentry.p0()
   // AARCH64:       %[[call:.*]] = call i32 @_setjmpex(ptr @jb, ptr %[[addr]])
   // AARCH64-NEXT:  ret i32 %[[call]]
+
+  // ARM32-LABEL: define dso_local arm_aapcs_vfpcc i32 @test_setjmp
+  // ARM32:       %[[addr:.*]] = call ptr @llvm.sponentry.p0()
+  // ARM32:       %[[call:.*]] = call arm_aapcs_vfpcc i32 @_setjmp(ptr @jb, ptr %[[addr]])
+  // ARM32-NEXT:  ret i32 %[[call]]
 }
 
 int test_setjmpex(void) {
@@ -41,4 +50,9 @@
   // AARCH64:       %[[addr:.*]] = call ptr @llvm.sponentry.p0()
   // AARCH64:       %[[call:.*]] = call i32 @_setjmpex(ptr @jb, ptr %[[addr]])
   // AARCH64-NEXT:  ret i32 %[[call]]
+
+  // ARM32-LABEL: define dso_local arm_aapcs_vfpcc i32 @test_setjmpex
+  // ARM32:       %[[addr:.*]] = call ptr @llvm.sponentry.p0()
+  // ARM32:       %[[call:.*]] = call arm_aapcs_vfpcc i32 @_setjmpex(ptr @jb, ptr %[[addr]])
+  // ARM32-NEXT:  ret i32 %[[call]]
 }
